; Unused code fragment: fill a 2x3 block of attribute cells
;
; Never executed and unreachable: it follows the unconditional JP $91C2 at the
; end of #R$91BE, and no jump, call or word in the image points to $93BB-$93D0.
; It starts with LD (HL),A, so it looks like the tail of a routine whose first
; part is not in the image; what it was called from is Unknown.
; .
; What it would do (checked by calling it in the simulator with HL=$58A5, A=2
; and $80A0=$38): the ink A is merged with the paper, bright and flash bits of
; the room's first tile attribute ($80A0, the background tile) and stored in
; the 2x3 block of attribute cells (2 wide, 3 high) whose top-left cell is HL:
; (HL), (HL+1), (HL+$20), (HL+$21), (HL+$40), (HL+$41). Result there: $3A in all
; six cells.
; .
; Hardware: writes screen attributes.
; .
; A Ink colour (bits 0-2)
; HL Attribute address of the top-left cell
@label=FillAttrBlock
c$93BB LD (HL),A     ;
 $93BC LD A,($80A0)  ; attribute of the room background tile
@isub=AND ATTR_INK_CLEAR
 $93BF AND $F8       ; keep paper, bright, flash
 $93C1 OR (HL)       ;
 $93C2 LD (HL),A     ;
@isub=LD DE,SCREEN_COLS-1
 $93C3 LD DE,$001F   ; with INC HL: next row, same column
 $93C6 INC HL        ;
 $93C7 LD (HL),A     ;
 $93C8 ADD HL,DE     ;
 $93C9 LD (HL),A     ;
 $93CA INC HL        ;
 $93CB LD (HL),A     ;
 $93CC ADD HL,DE     ;
 $93CD LD (HL),A     ;
 $93CE INC HL        ;
 $93CF LD (HL),A     ;
 $93D0 RET           ;
